WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:02.313
- My ability to fool other people.

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:05.880
Cause it's a game, right?

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:09.240
You're playing a game and
everyone's trying to be someone

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:12.240
and the better you can
pretend to be someone,

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:16.230
is as good as a it'll
ever look to someone else.

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:18.300
I don't know who I am in the end of it.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:19.844
Which is interesting 'cause I don't know,

00:00:19.844 --> 00:00:22.980
you know, you expect to be
a certain kind of person,

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:24.270
you think you're a certain kind of person,

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:27.780
and when you don't know,
then you're confused,

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:29.180
and you're messing yourself.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.530
- I'm a drug addict, like straight up.

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:38.070
Like, I'm sober now, but I've been,

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:39.840
I've struggled with drugs in the past

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.720
and I, you know, like I work on it,

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:44.340
but it's something that
really scares me about myself.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:46.290
'Cause I know how
self-destructive I can be

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:47.490
and I know that like, if I don't keep

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:49.890
on working on this problem I have,

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:52.350
then eventually I will
just like self-destruct

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:53.823
and possibly kill myself, so.

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:59.700
- My anger, my anger scares me.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:00.750
- [Interviewer] Can you give us an example

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:03.390
of a time where your anger scared you.

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:06.090
Yeah, like I found out my
boyfriend was cheating on me

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:09.510
and I was afraid I might kill the girl.

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:10.343
- [Interviewer] You were what?

00:01:10.343 --> 00:01:11.800
- I was afraid I might kill her.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:13.863
Not like murder.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:16.490
That scared me, you know?

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:22.260
- The thing that scares me
about myself is how easily

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:26.520
and fast I get attached to things

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:31.520
and ideas of things and
ideas of people slash people.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:36.800
Let's say, let's say you
start talking to somebody,

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:38.580
as soon as you start talking to somebody

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:41.100
and they give you the most
little bit of attention,

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.290
boom, I'm attached.

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:48.290
Come here, let's talk more,
let's hang out, like literally.

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:52.620
Same with friends too like
second I meet somebody,

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:54.363
if we match energies, boom.

00:01:55.336 --> 00:01:57.000
We're connected.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.703
You're now part of me, kind of situation.

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:03.990
- I guess that like your upbringing

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:06.540
and experiences and everything negative

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:09.390
that happens to you
defines you as a person.

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:13.200
And I forget that I'm 1000% judged

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.120
on what I've done in the past

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:17.910
and my wrongdoings, my shortcomings.

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:21.090
So I would say being defined by

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:23.552
the things that make me vulnerable.

00:02:23.552 --> 00:02:24.385
Yeah.

00:02:24.385 --> 00:02:26.100
- [Interviewer] Is this
something you think about often?

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.410
- Oh, probably every day.

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:32.223
Yeah, I think I struggle
with opening up, yeah.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:33.953
- My future.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:36.540
That's what I would say.

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:38.370
I don't have any like future plans.

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:39.930
I don't really know myself too well

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:44.930
so I don't really have anything
to look forward to, I guess.

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:48.720
- What scares me the most about myself

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:50.490
is that I can do anything that I want.

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:53.523
Like I'm the luckiest
person alive, I think.

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:55.800
I would love to do a lot of simple things

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:58.020
and then I'd like do a
lot of complicated things.

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:00.030
I would love to be a chemist.

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:01.800
I'd love to be an environmental engineer.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:05.190
I'd love to learn about algae and oysters.

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:07.320
I love to be a leaf.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.730
I'd like to be a tree.

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:10.680
I'd like to be an elephant.

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:12.630
Anyway, yeah.

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:15.557
- [Interviewer] So the
fact that you could,

00:03:15.557 --> 00:03:19.020
in your mind, you could
be any of these things

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:22.267
and you can't decide,
that's what scares you most?

00:03:22.267 --> 00:03:23.287
- Yeah.

00:03:23.287 --> 00:03:25.053
Yeah, I'm scared to decide.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:29.070
- I find it really hard to focus.

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:31.740
Probably like every three
months I shift gears

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:33.480
and this is my thing now.

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:36.600
And then it lasts three months.

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:38.640
Right now it's sailing.

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:39.473
- [Interviewer] Sailing?

00:03:39.473 --> 00:03:40.306
- Sailing.

00:03:40.306 --> 00:03:44.340
Yeah, I just bought a boat in
Mexico for not enough money.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:45.750
It's a really boat.

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:47.400
- [Interviewer] How long ago
did you get into sailing?

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.273
- About three months ago.

00:03:49.273 --> 00:03:51.990
(both laughing)

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:53.220
- [Interviewer] You
have me thinking though,

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:56.280
like why do we feel like we
have to stick with one thing

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:57.840
our whole life like
why not do what you do?

00:03:57.840 --> 00:03:59.290
- Because I'm a really saver

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:03.280
and I'm not a particularly
good anything else either.

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:08.220
But I know a little bit about a lot of

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:10.770
it's not very useful to anybody though.

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:11.820
- [Interviewer] Okay.

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:16.740
- I'm scared that deep
down I think that I know

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:19.060
I won't do what I want to do with my life

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:23.010
and I think that's what scares me most.

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:26.460
I don't know, maybe I've
been told that by a lot

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:30.483
of people that I won't make it
and that I'm not good enough.

00:04:32.697 --> 00:04:33.963
- I'm not scared anymore.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:37.830
I used to be scared but
I'm not scared anymore.

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:38.867
That's my answer.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:43.989
- I think I have trouble figuring out

00:04:43.989 --> 00:04:46.950
when to be guilty and when not to be

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:49.290
and when it should make
sense and when it shouldn't.

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:51.900
I often get a lot of guilt put on me

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:54.090
and I handle it weirdly.

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:55.860
I just feel like I'm blamed for stuff

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:57.870
more than I should sometimes.

00:04:57.870 --> 00:05:02.870
And so, I don't know if
I need to work on myself

00:05:04.173 --> 00:05:07.953
or if I shouldn't take the
blame as much, I guess.

00:05:08.803 --> 00:05:11.310
- I feel like I'm
stressed out all the time

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:13.410
and like my brain kind of goes

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:15.720
at like a million miles a minute

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:18.450
and like I can never really turn it off.

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:20.950
And I think that I worry
that I'll never like

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:24.960
know like a full peace with myself

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:27.060
and like be able to just
sit down with myself

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:29.604
and like feel good being silent

00:05:29.604 --> 00:05:31.950
and like alone and like not feel the need

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:33.420
to be doing a million things at once

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:35.610
or like anxious about everything.

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:37.433
- [Interviewer] Have you ever felt peace?

00:05:39.742 --> 00:05:40.992
- I don't know.

00:05:43.890 --> 00:05:45.660
- As much as we want to believe

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:49.080
that we know ourselves
more than anybody else,

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:54.080
there is so much unpredictability,
infinitely, actually.

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:58.320
We are not the same person two seconds ago

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:00.540
that we are two seconds later.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:02.310
Without our permission.

00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:04.010
And I think that's what scares me.

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:09.510
- I feel like every day
I'm a different person

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:13.890
and every day I have a
different set of morals

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:17.730
and things that I know
are true about myself.

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:20.760
But the next day I'll think about

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:22.760
the decisions I've made the previous day

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:27.033
and I'll realize that that's not who I am.

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:32.913
But I really don't know if it
is who I am or if it isn't.

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:38.750
Because I think like,
when I'm doing something

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:45.260
I'm doing it mostly just
based on like what feels right

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:50.010
because I've been told that
that's like the way to live.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:53.520
But what feels right is not
always good for everyone.

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:57.970
And I think what I'm most
scared about myself is

00:06:59.970 --> 00:07:02.670
how I harm people without knowing

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:05.070
and how that affects not just them

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:06.630
but another person that they know

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:07.830
and another person that they know

00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:09.663
and ultimately like the world.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:15.530
And just not realizing
the weight of my actions.

00:07:17.130 --> 00:07:18.840
Even the smallest actions.

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:23.520
And I guess overall not
having self-control.

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:25.860
Yeah, that is really, it's really scary

00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:30.860
and it's really hard and I
don't really have anything

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:33.420
that I feel like I'm loyal to.

00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:38.220
Like I don't have a set of
morals that I'm loyal to.

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:42.420
And because I like grew up like atheist

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:44.853
and so I know most people like,

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:48.330
it's just a part of their existence

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:52.830
to have like certain beliefs
and for me it's very ambiguous

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:55.203
and like there are many possibilities.

00:07:56.130 --> 00:08:01.130
And I think that's why it's so
hard for me to center myself

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:04.830
and really see what is
true to me and what isn't.

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:07.080
And so I think the only
way that I can learn

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:10.560
is through experience
and a lot of mistakes

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:14.130
and a lot of damage,
which I don't want to do

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:18.543
but I have no other way of learning, so.

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:20.243
Yeah.

00:08:21.420 --> 00:08:23.070
- When I know that I want something

00:08:23.070 --> 00:08:25.863
and I don't just do everything for it.

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:28.490
- [Interviewer] Why is that your answer?

00:08:28.490 --> 00:08:30.071
Is this something you've
been thinking about?

00:08:30.071 --> 00:08:31.238
- A lot, yeah.

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:37.140
I recently like met a stranger
who gave me this long speech

00:08:37.140 --> 00:08:41.880
about like if you know
your passion go for it

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:43.560
and if you don't go for
it you're gonna regret it

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:44.580
for the rest of your life.

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:49.580
And I literally had just
decided I'm gonna give up on it

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:54.540
and the potential to not chase what I know

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:57.480
that I want is really scary.

00:08:57.480 --> 00:08:59.160
- [Interviewer] Where'd
you meet the stranger?

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:02.820
- I was on a flight and I got moved

00:09:02.820 --> 00:09:05.640
actually to randomly sit next to him

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:09.450
and it was just an old guy
and he just started talking

00:09:09.450 --> 00:09:12.093
and it was just a divine intervention.

00:09:13.710 --> 00:09:17.670
I'm an artist and I wanna be a musician

00:09:17.670 --> 00:09:22.410
and I had just like, I'm a sociology major

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:24.346
and I had just decided to like hunker down

00:09:24.346 --> 00:09:27.393
and just like give up and stuff like,

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:30.810
doing the thing that I love
and the thing that I wake up

00:09:30.810 --> 00:09:33.240
and think about every second of my life.

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:37.417
And then, I was talking
to him and he was like,

00:09:37.417 --> 00:09:39.390
"Why would you not?"

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:40.650
- [Interviewer] Yeah, why would you not?

00:09:40.650 --> 00:09:44.430
- Because I'm never gonna
be the best in the room

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:46.930
but I'm also never gonna
be the worst in the room.

00:09:48.546 --> 00:09:52.470
And I let myself like be scared of people

00:09:52.470 --> 00:09:54.540
who are better than me
rather than be inspired

00:09:54.540 --> 00:09:56.010
by people who are better than me.

00:09:56.010 --> 00:10:00.390
And I don't know, it's just
something I need to stop doing

00:10:00.390 --> 00:10:04.620
and I just need to focus
on doing the thing.

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:07.140
- [Interviewer] Where
can you find your reason?

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:08.258
- Oh my.

00:10:08.258 --> 00:10:10.773
I, nowhere I, my bedroom.

00:10:12.870 --> 00:10:13.703
Sorry.

00:10:13.703 --> 00:10:14.536
- [Interviewer] It's okay.

